Upstream work
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
model/motionbricks_mlx/ is a port to Apple MLX of MotionBricks
(https://github.com/NVlabs/motionbricks, v0.2.0, commit 54fc563):

    Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES. All rights reserved.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Files carrying the header "MLX port of MotionBricks" were translated from the
upstream PyTorch sources (tools/onnx/models/**) and modified: re-implemented in
MLX with a channels-last tensor layout, unified SOMA/G1 code paths, and added
compilation, reduced-precision and quantization options.

model-rs/ is a Rust port of model/motionbricks_mlx (files carrying the header "Rust
port of motionbricks_mlx"): an op-for-op port on mlx-rs, and a model-specific Metal
runtime with its own Metal kernels. Its GEMM kernel follows the tiling scheme of MLX's
steel GEMM (fragment layout, interleaved simdgroup tiles, serpentine accumulation);
MLX is MIT-licensed, Copyright © 2023 Apple Inc., and is not redistributed here.
model/motionbricks_mlx/assets/rig_kernels.metal holds Metal transcriptions of the
upstream rig geometry, shared by both ports.

MotionBricks paper: T. Wang et al., "MotionBricks: Scalable Real-Time Motions with
Modular Latent Generative Model and Smart Primitives", ACM TOG 45(4), 2026.

